          Updated November 21, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#spirit-xt485"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41-4F7a-pkL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Spirit XT485" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#spirit-xt285"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41SHoChUzvL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Spirit XT285" width="458" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-7-4-at"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wMaZFsNwL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon 7.4 AT" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Spirit XT485 · Spirit XT285 · Horizon 7.4 AT</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          The treadmills with the longest home warranty are Spirit&rsquo;s XT485 and XT285: lifetime cover on
          the frame, motor and deck, and ten years on parts, on Spirit&rsquo;s own pages when we checked on
          21 November 2026. Horizon&rsquo;s 7.4 AT is the strongest warranty under $1,500 on Amazon, with
          lifetime frame and motor, five years on parts and two years of labour. Below that, the
          &ldquo;lifetime&rdquo; headline hides big differences: the Horizon T101 Connect and the Sole F65
          both promise lifetime frame and motor, but the T101&rsquo;s parts and labour run for one year.
          We have not tested these treadmills hands-on. Warranty terms come from each maker&rsquo;s site,
          dated, and specifications from the maker or the Amazon listing.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
